<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antisuyu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anti Suyu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antisuyu was the north-eastern quarter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>, covering the eastern slopes of the Andes and the edge of the Amazonian forest beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a>. Its name is often thought to be the origin of the word Andes. The Incas held it with frontier forts against the forest peoples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antisuyu.jpg" alt="Antisuyu" width="250" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TawantinSuyu_AntiSuyu.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
